From f465addca88c648629e5c31c00d995e55321e5fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 10:14:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Add symbol filter and per-factor breakdown to the scan
 log

/api/logs and the dashboard's scan log table only showed the
composite score and a text rejection reason, with no way to isolate
one symbol (e.g. NIFTY 50) or see which of the nine confluence
factors actually failed.

- ScanLog gains a `factors` JSON column storing the same per-factor
  score dict filters.py already computes (direction, squeeze, volume,
  adx, rsi, structure, sweep, oi, htf, composite, composite_all).
  Picked up automatically by the existing in-place column migration;
  old rows read back with factors=None.
- scanner.py's _log_scan now records that dict on every scan, not
  just the composite number.
- /api/logs and the dashboard accept an optional `symbol` query param
  (comma-separated, e.g. ?symbol=NIFTY%2050,BANKNIFTY) that filters
  the scan log to just those symbols.
- The dashboard's scan log table gets a "Factors" column rendering
  the same pass/half/fail chips already used on the signals table,
  plus a filter box above the table wired to the new query param.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
